  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f69c6b1f1e1fc2c4b9a85c7696ada520, type: 3}
  m_Name: AfterTutor1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogSO
  replics:
  - Hey. Why are you sitting behind that crate?
  - "Oh, nothing. Just trying to figure out what my \u201Cex\u201D husband is doing
    without me."
  - Ex? Then why is he still wearing his ring?
  - " \u2026Are you serious?"
  - "Yep. Guess you\u2019re not very observant."
  - "That\u2019s it? Anything else?"
  - "He also keeps your photos everywhere he can. Why are you asking me instead of
    him? And you\u2019re not wearing your ring either."
  - "You really don\u2019t get it? You\u2019re not a kid anymore. If we\u2019re fighting,
    that means there\u2019s a reason."
  - "If he blamed me for \u201Cchoosing the wrong path,\u201D then why is he here
    too? He should earn me back and prove he loves me."
  - "How old are you\u2026 32? That is an incredibly childish stance.."
  - And what would you do then?
  - "Well, first of all \u2014 I wouldn\u2019t end up in that situation. Second\u2026
    if we\u2019re talking hypothetically, if I were arguing with someone\u2026 "
  - " I\u2019d just tell them directly what I don\u2019t like and what I want. And
    then they can do whatever they want, because until I like the result, I won\u2019t
    forgive them."
  - "Don\u2019t you think that\u2019s too simple?"
  - "No. Because if someone screws up, my standards are high and fixed. And if they
    don\u2019t meet th\u0435\u2014"
  - "Stop, stop, stop. A person is one thing \u2014 a lover is another."
  - "Uh\u2026 well\u2026 I\u2019ve, uhm\u2026 never had that kind of\u2026 situation.I
    mean um\u2026\u201DLover\u201D."
  - "But\u2026 if someone cheated on me, I\u2019d probably do everything possible
    to ruin that\u2026 \u201Clover\u2019s\u201D life."
  - See? Now you do understand me. And you actually know how to get embarrassed,
    huh.
  - "Ew. No. That was purely hypothetical. And you two are fighting because of work\u2026
    deal with your own problems."
  - "All you do is whine. And honestly, if something bothers you, either set him
    on fire or talk it out. We\u2019re practically in slavery anyway\u2014nothing\u2019s
    changing."
  - "Heh-heh\u2026 so you do get it."
